  {
   "id": 242808,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/a1294008e6e2e075.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work from BioNinja)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The pyramid on the left shows the population numbers of primary producers, and primary, secondary and tertiary consumers. The pyramid on the right gives their biomass.</p>\n<p>Which option decribes this ecosystem?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 760693,
     "content_html": "A grassland where primary producers are grasses."
    },
    {
     "id": 760692,
     "content_html": "A desert environment where the primary producers are short bushes."
    },
    {
     "id": 760691,
     "content_html": "A coral reef where the primary producers are the corals."
    },
    {
     "id": 760694,
     "content_html": "A mature forest where the primary producers are large trees."
    }
